# GameTrack API

This repository contains the NestJS backend for GameTrack. Its sibling
frontend is maintained independently at:
https://github.com/LucasCruz2773/game-tracker-web

Use Node.js 24. Do not downgrade it or change the configured engine/version
unless explicitly requested.

## Architecture

- NestJS, TypeScript, PostgreSQL and Prisma
- REST API with Swagger/OpenAPI
- Google OAuth and JWT session in an httpOnly cookie
- Domain modules: auth, users, games, library and reviews
- Controllers handle HTTP concerns; services contain business logic
- Validate all external input and never expose secrets or token data
- The API is the integration layer for external game providers such as RAWG

The OpenAPI document is the source of truth for the frontend contract. Avoid
breaking response or endpoint changes. When one is necessary, coordinate it
with a corresponding branch and pull request in the web repository.

## Development

- Build incrementally; do not add future infrastructure without a concrete use
- Preserve strict typing and avoid `any`
- Add meaningful unit/integration tests for business rules
- Do not rewrite unrelated code
- Keep `.env` untracked and document configuration in `.env.example`
- Before adding a dependency, confirm current stable support for Node.js 24

Use small Conventional Commits, for example `feat(library): add status filter`.
Run Git commands in this repository, not in the parent workspace.

Current priority: keep the existing MVP production-ready before adding social,
queue, recommendation or AI features.
